TaijiOS APE Linux-source compatibility
======================================

This layer is for source compatibility with portable Linux/POSIX programs. It is
not a Linux binary ABI.

Use:

	ape/taiji-posix-sh
	linuxcc file.c -o file

The profile enables:

	-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L
	-D_BSD_EXTENSION
	-D_TAIJI_POSIX_SOURCE

Supported additions include poll(2), clock_gettime(2), nanosleep(2), basic
terminal window-size ioctls, getline(3), getdelim(3), pipe2(2), *at directory
helpers for normal paths, aligned allocation helpers, and common glibc string
helpers.

Unsupported Linux-only facilities intentionally fail with ENOSYS:

	mmap/munmap/mprotect/msync
	epoll_create/epoll_ctl/epoll_wait
	inotify_init/inotify_add_watch/inotify_rm_watch
	eventfd/eventfd_read/eventfd_write
	timerfd_create/timerfd_settime/timerfd_gettime
	signalfd

TUI programs should prefer termios, ANSI/vt100 escapes, poll/select, and
TIOCGWINSZ. The default compatibility terminal size is 80x24 until the active
terminal can report dynamic geometry.

For Linux binaries, use `linuxrun -n file` to inspect the ELF header and
program-header load plan without trying to execute it. `linuxrun file [args]`
provides experimental i386 Linux ELF execution, separately from APE.
`linuxrun -e NAME=value` supplies a guest environment entry. The native
`linux-app` launcher integrates selected Debian X11 applications into the
desktop; see /doc/unified-desktop.md for setup, checks, and limitations.
